# Stock Market Data Analysis and Prediction\n\nThis Jupyter notebook contains steps to explore the synthetic stock data, build a simple neural network model for price prediction, and visualize the results.\n\n```python\n# Stock Market Data Analysis and Prediction\n\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\nimport tensorflow as tf\nfrom tensorflow.keras import layers\n\n# Load data\ndf = pd.read_csv('../data/stock_data.csv')\n\n# Convert Date column to datetime\ndf['Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Date'])\n\n# Plot Closing Price\nplt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\ndf['Close'].plot(title='Close Price History')\nplt.xlabel('Date')\nplt.ylabel('Close Price')\nplt.show()\n\n# Feature Engineering\ndf['Target'] = df['Close'].shift(-1)  # Next day's close\ndf.dropna(inplace=True)\nX = df[['Open', 'High', 'Low', 'Close', 'Volume']].values\ny = df['Target'].values\n\n# Scale features\nscaler = MinMaxScaler()\nX_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\n\n# Train-test split\nX_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X_scaled, y, test_size=0.2, shuffle=False)\n\n# Build neural network\nmodel = tf.keras.Sequential([\n    layers.Dense(64, activation='relu', input_shape=(X_train.shape[1],)),\n    layers.Dense(32, activation='relu'),\n    layers.Dense(1)\n])\n\nmodel.compile(optimizer='adam', loss='mse')\n\n# Train model\nhistory = model.fit(X_train, y_train, epochs=20, validation_split=0.2)\n\n# Predict\npreds = model.predict(X_test)\n\n# Evaluate\nrmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, preds))\nprint(f'RMSE: {rmse:.2f}')\n\n# Plot predictions vs actual\nplt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\nplt.plot(y_test, label='Actual')\nplt.plot(preds, label='Predicted')\nplt.legend()\nplt.title('Prediction vs Actual')\nplt.show()\n```\n\nFeel free to enhance this notebook with additional analyses, feature engineering, or alte